<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Buxar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1764</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Buxar was fought in October 1764 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> army under Hector Munro and the combined forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mir-qasim">Mir Qasim</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shuja-ud-daula">Shuja-ud-Daula</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a> and the Mughal emperor Shah Alam II. The British victory led to the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Allahabad</a> of 1765, by which the Company gained the diwani, the right to collect the revenue of Bengal, Bihar and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-buxar.jpg" alt="Battle of Buxar" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Martin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Hector_Munro_by_David_Martin_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
